- A CLI that surfaces logs from the database. ~/.mucka/mucka.db holds every session's raw wire
  traffic (sessions/wire) and every encounter's classified rows, and nothing in the client reads
  either back. WireLogExport.ListSessions/ReadSession are the seed - they have no other caller.
  Wanted: list sessions, dump one as text, and grep the encounter tables. See
  docs/persistence-design.md, "What an offline reader takes".
- A parsed `lines` table, with the C1 code that introduced each line. StyledLine carries only
  LineKind (four values); the code lives in the parser and never leaves it, so a code-level question
  still has to re-parse wire.data. Storing it means surfacing the code from Mud2C1Decoder's
  dispatch sites onto StyledLine.
- Optimize input handling performance (no chug/lag),
- Make the 'compass' a compass,
- Chat panel?
- Right-click context menu with "Copy" or "Dictionary" for individual words?
- ResetClock: re-derive the FES-suppression model from the wire. The engine assumes a ~500ms
  server rate limit; the corpus contradicts a time-based cause (547 stats-container pairs land
  <500ms apart, 58 under 250ms, two probes sent in the same millisecond were both answered).
  Clio's FES.md says the score packet is sent when a stat CHANGES. LogResetDiagnostics defaults
  to false, so the theory cannot be falsified in normal use.
- Combat: the 07 "isolated hit" family (bites/stings/kicks/throws) is unparsed, so a wyvern's
  venomous tail sting - real damage, its own code, its own "Stamina=N/M." line - is invisible to
  per-fight stats.
- Combat rail: CombatTierResolver.CriticalStaminaFloorTier (the "no lower than T2 at or below
  6.5 stamina" floor in docs/combat-panel-design.md) exists and is tested but nothing calls it;
  SidePanelViewModel feeds the stamina tier straight to ResolvePulseTier.
- Invisible opponents: a creature that fades BEFORE the player engages it has no name to recover, so
  the fight opens against "someone" (on the wire: a man faded while fighting a fox, and `k man` a
  minute later answered "You attack someone."). CombatTracker's _faded set is encounter-scoped and
  cannot see it. Naming it needs a registry of which invisible creatures are in THIS room, which
  belongs with RoomCreatures rather than with the tracker. Mortal invisibility (C1 05.00.05) is
  untagged for the same reason it is unhandled: no capture of a player doing it mid-fight.
- Combat: "The thief takes back his offer to withdraw from your fight." (verbatim) is unparsed. It
  retracts a NpcWithdrawOffer, which is not an end either, so nothing is currently wrong - but a
  panel that ever draws a standing offer would keep drawing it after it was withdrawn.
- Any "$" or "^" line is client-local on both platforms, including at MUD2's persona password
  prompt, where it is echoed into scrollback and history and never sent. There is no escape
  hatch for sending one to the MUD.
